<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Nov consumer prices rise 0.1 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Nov consumer prices rise 0.1 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumer prices in the Tokyo area in November rose 0.1 percent from a year earlier, while nationwide consumer prices in October rose 0.5 percent from a year before, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of consumer prices, for Tokyo and nationwide (index base 1995):</p>
<p>				    NOV	  OCT	  SEPT</p>
<p> Tokyo overall index	  99.8	100.1	100.0</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr change	    +0.1 pct    0.0 pct   -0.4 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth change	  -0.3 pct   +0.1 pct   +0.2 pct</p>
<p> Tokyo core index	    100.1	100.1	100.0</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr change	    -0.1 pct   -0.1 pct   -0.3 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth change	   0.0 pct   +0.1 pct   +0.3 pct</p>
<p>				   OCT	 SEPT	  AUG</p>
<p> Nationwide overall index 100.6	100.4	100.0</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr change	    +0.5 pct   0.0 pct   +0.2 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth change	  +0.2 pct  +0.4 pct   -0.1 pct</p>
<p> Nationwide core index    100.5	100.4	 99.9</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr change	    +0.2 pct   +0.2 pct   +0.2 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth change	  +0.1 pct   +0.5 pct   -0.2 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: Tokyo index calculated by collecting price data at mid-month. Core indices are overall prices minus fresh food prices.</p>
</text>
